WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.185 --> 00:00:02.403
- Good morning believe nation
my name is Evan Carmichael

00:00:02.403 --> 00:00:03.653
my one word is believe

00:00:03.653 --> 00:00:05.376
and I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:05.376 --> 00:00:07.639
will solve all of the
world's major problems.

00:00:07.639 --> 00:00:10.066
So to help you on your
journey today's message

00:00:10.066 --> 00:00:13.278
is discomfort is your friend.

00:00:13.278 --> 00:00:15.050
Over to you Joe Rogan.

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.341
(rooster crows)

00:00:17.341 --> 00:00:19.849
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.849 --> 00:00:22.439
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:25.939
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:26.863 --> 00:00:29.828
- Our bodies for whatever reason

00:00:29.828 --> 00:00:31.306
most people their associations

00:00:31.306 --> 00:00:34.551
are to avoid anything that's uncomfortable

00:00:34.551 --> 00:00:36.645
but it's so illogical

00:00:36.645 --> 00:00:38.906
because when you look at comfort

00:00:38.906 --> 00:00:41.356
and you look at success and progress

00:00:41.356 --> 00:00:45.224
and the eventual feelings
of accomplishment

00:00:45.224 --> 00:00:47.821
and of getting past certain hurtles

00:00:47.821 --> 00:00:50.328
in terms of how you feel about life.

00:00:50.328 --> 00:00:53.125
A lot of those are
connected to discomfort.

00:00:53.125 --> 00:00:54.811
Discomfort is your friend.

00:00:54.811 --> 00:00:55.757
It really is.

00:00:55.757 --> 00:00:59.257
Discomfort and not being happy and content

00:01:00.245 --> 00:01:02.056
with certain situations in life

00:01:02.056 --> 00:01:03.415
or certain feelings in life,

00:01:03.415 --> 00:01:05.748
there are massive motivators

00:01:07.035 --> 00:01:10.535
and they're amazing at facilitating change

00:01:11.392 --> 00:01:15.217
and yet our instinct is to avoid those

00:01:15.217 --> 00:01:16.406
and just sit on the couch

00:01:16.406 --> 00:01:20.071
and watch some reality show
about dudes who make moonshine

00:01:20.071 --> 00:01:22.410
with our jaw open like (gurgles)

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:24.218
it's bizarre.

00:01:24.218 --> 00:01:25.656
- You can measure your growth in life

00:01:25.656 --> 00:01:27.998
as a human being by how much discomfort

00:01:27.998 --> 00:01:30.342
you're regularly experiencing.

00:01:30.342 --> 00:01:32.112
There's that old expression that you need

00:01:32.112 --> 00:01:33.264
to scare yourself everyday.

00:01:33.264 --> 00:01:34.708
Right we hear it in songs.

00:01:34.708 --> 00:01:36.315
We hear it in radio.

00:01:36.315 --> 00:01:37.148
We hear it on TV.

00:01:37.148 --> 00:01:38.208
We read it in books.

00:01:38.208 --> 00:01:40.020
You got to do something
that scares you every day

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.048
and it's great advice.

00:01:41.048 --> 00:01:42.732
It's amazing advice.

00:01:42.732 --> 00:01:44.912
We just don't do it.

00:01:44.912 --> 00:01:46.639
Do you do something that
scares you everyday?

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.077
When was the last time you did something

00:01:48.077 --> 00:01:50.631
that actually scares you?

00:01:50.631 --> 00:01:52.644
When you aren't doing
things that scare you

00:01:52.644 --> 00:01:54.991
that's when you see insane growth.

00:01:54.991 --> 00:01:56.511
That's when you see yourself developing,

00:01:56.511 --> 00:01:57.953
your business developing

00:01:57.953 --> 00:01:59.769
and it may not happen right away

00:01:59.769 --> 00:02:02.119
but through that process
of scaring yourself

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:03.930
and getting uncomfortable,

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.773
that's when you start
seeing amazing things happen

00:02:06.773 --> 00:02:08.009
and you feel great.

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:10.227
You feel scared but you also feel great

00:02:10.227 --> 00:02:11.749
because we love to grow

00:02:11.749 --> 00:02:12.982
'cause as humans we want to grow.

00:02:12.982 --> 00:02:13.815
We want to get better.

00:02:13.815 --> 00:02:14.648
We want to learn.

00:02:14.648 --> 00:02:15.658
We want to develop ourselves

00:02:15.658 --> 00:02:16.932
and so what I would encourage you to do is

00:02:16.932 --> 00:02:19.094
try to develop the habit

00:02:19.094 --> 00:02:21.690
of you can either consciously say

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.826
I'm tryin' to do somethin'
to scare myself everyday.

00:02:23.826 --> 00:02:24.659
Right?

00:02:24.659 --> 00:02:25.492
Which can be a good practice

00:02:25.492 --> 00:02:27.367
but also can be reactive

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:30.326
in that when you have an idea

00:02:30.326 --> 00:02:32.060
or somebody asks you to do something

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.380
and you get those nerves.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:34.286
Right?

00:02:34.286 --> 00:02:37.000
You get those nerves that scare you.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:40.050
I don't want to do that I might fail.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:44.623
To recognize that and then
to build and grow from that.

00:02:44.623 --> 00:02:47.500
To start building that muscle of fear

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.308
and breaking through it.

00:02:49.308 --> 00:02:50.456
I think it's really important.

00:02:50.456 --> 00:02:52.922
I think most of what
we do is subconscious.

00:02:52.922 --> 00:02:55.185
I think most of the actions
you take will be subconscious.

00:02:55.185 --> 00:02:57.741
You will just naturally play smaller

00:02:57.741 --> 00:03:00.167
without even thinking about it.

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:02.102
You'll rationalize the fear.

00:03:02.102 --> 00:03:02.935
Right?

00:03:02.935 --> 00:03:05.066
You'll rationalize the discomfort.

00:03:05.066 --> 00:03:07.819
You really want to start a YouTube channel

00:03:07.819 --> 00:03:08.927
and the real reason is you're afraid

00:03:08.927 --> 00:03:10.736
to get in front of the camera.

00:03:10.736 --> 00:03:13.042
You're afraid of people's judgment of you

00:03:13.042 --> 00:03:14.522
but instead of recognizing that

00:03:14.522 --> 00:03:16.910
you'll say oh but I don't have the money,

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:17.854
just to get a camera.

00:03:17.854 --> 00:03:18.687
I don't have the time.

00:03:18.687 --> 00:03:19.520
I have a really busy life

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:20.650
and you know I got to get the gear

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:21.804
and the lights, the microphone

00:03:21.804 --> 00:03:22.955
and I don't know even know if I need

00:03:22.955 --> 00:03:24.536
to go to school for this.

00:03:24.536 --> 00:03:26.004
All the irrationalize the reason

00:03:26.004 --> 00:03:28.019
but deep down it's just fear.

00:03:28.019 --> 00:03:28.852
You're just afraid.

00:03:28.852 --> 00:03:31.028
So the first step is just understanding

00:03:31.028 --> 00:03:33.083
that it's fear.

00:03:33.083 --> 00:03:35.960
That you're really just
afraid of doing this thing

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:38.221
and then when you understand that,

00:03:38.221 --> 00:03:42.221
practice developing the
courage to go and do it.

00:03:43.317 --> 00:03:46.118
Whenever I feel myself
being a little bit afraid,

00:03:46.118 --> 00:03:47.967
worried about other people's expectations,

00:03:47.967 --> 00:03:49.860
then I know I have to go up and do it.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:50.766
So a couple examples,

00:03:50.766 --> 00:03:53.113
I went to Paris not that long ago

00:03:53.113 --> 00:03:55.416
and was speaking on stage
at a key note speech

00:03:55.416 --> 00:03:57.296
to close out a conference.

00:03:57.296 --> 00:03:59.600
There's about 2000 people in the room

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.688
and I've done tons of
these speeches right?

00:04:02.688 --> 00:04:04.128
I've done a lot of speeches

00:04:04.128 --> 00:04:06.184
and every time I go I want to try

00:04:06.184 --> 00:04:07.132
and do something new.

00:04:07.132 --> 00:04:07.965
Something different.

00:04:07.965 --> 00:04:08.798
Not just for the audience,

00:04:08.798 --> 00:04:10.424
'cause a lot of the audience
hadn't seen me before.

00:04:10.424 --> 00:04:12.111
For myself.

00:04:12.111 --> 00:04:14.746
I don't want to get up on stage
and just do the same speech

00:04:14.746 --> 00:04:16.842
that I've always done.

00:04:16.842 --> 00:04:20.776
Every time I go I want to do
something different for myself

00:04:20.776 --> 00:04:23.733
and so this time I went up
and I didn't use any slides.

00:04:23.733 --> 00:04:26.036
I had one slide the entire presentation.

00:04:26.036 --> 00:04:28.299
Usually I had slides
that would have pictures,

00:04:28.299 --> 00:04:30.724
I'd follow it along the
story of what I was saying.

00:04:30.724 --> 00:04:32.498
I don't read from slides
I've never done that.

00:04:32.498 --> 00:04:34.267
Well maybe probably when I
started a bit from slides

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:36.527
but this time I was like you know what

00:04:36.527 --> 00:04:38.007
I have a 20 minute presentation.

00:04:38.007 --> 00:04:41.049
I'm going to get on the stage.

00:04:41.049 --> 00:04:42.323
I'm just going to go.

00:04:42.323 --> 00:04:43.887
And the initial fears that come back

00:04:43.887 --> 00:04:46.599
like what if I forget
what I'm going to say?

00:04:46.599 --> 00:04:48.242
What if I lose track?

00:04:48.242 --> 00:04:51.369
Because the pictures at
least kept me on track

00:04:51.369 --> 00:04:53.873
and what if I miss a point?

00:04:53.873 --> 00:04:54.706
You know.

00:04:55.564 --> 00:04:56.630
I shouldn't do it you know,

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:58.071
I've been paid to come here

00:04:58.071 --> 00:04:59.959
and I need to make sure I'm
providing a lot of value

00:04:59.959 --> 00:05:01.440
and that's maybe not the smartest idea.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:02.922
All of these fears come in.

00:05:02.922 --> 00:05:03.912
Like no I'm going to do it.

00:05:03.912 --> 00:05:05.352
I got to do it.

00:05:05.352 --> 00:05:07.167
I need to push myself for me

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:09.062
and I was so nervous

00:05:09.062 --> 00:05:11.038
there was a guy speaking before me

00:05:11.038 --> 00:05:14.450
I just couldn't wait for him to finish

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:16.343
'cause all the way
through his presentation,

00:05:16.343 --> 00:05:18.112
I'm thinking okay what am I going to say?

00:05:18.112 --> 00:05:19.515
I got to say this, I got to say this.

00:05:19.515 --> 00:05:21.323
Fears, fears, fears, fears.

00:05:21.323 --> 00:05:22.554
They announce my name

00:05:22.554 --> 00:05:24.528
instead of walkin' around the stage

00:05:24.528 --> 00:05:25.883
like everybody else does

00:05:25.883 --> 00:05:27.527
I just jumped onto the stage.

00:05:27.527 --> 00:05:28.558
I was in the front row.

00:05:28.558 --> 00:05:29.391
Evan Carmichael.

00:05:29.391 --> 00:05:31.229
I jumped on the stage and the MC

00:05:31.229 --> 00:05:33.330
had to come and shake my hand upfront

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.605
instead of around the side.

00:05:34.605 --> 00:05:36.172
I think it's important.

00:05:36.172 --> 00:05:38.436
I think it's important for yourself.

00:05:38.436 --> 00:05:41.893
That you do the things that
make you feel uncomfortable.

00:05:41.893 --> 00:05:43.588
I told this story before on my channel.

00:05:43.588 --> 00:05:45.438
Even making videos here

00:05:45.438 --> 00:05:47.497
I'm worried about people walking behind me

00:05:47.497 --> 00:05:49.392
and doin' it in a public setting instead

00:05:49.392 --> 00:05:51.737
of closing the doors
or doing somewhere else

00:05:51.737 --> 00:05:53.591
or wearing different colored socks

00:05:53.591 --> 00:05:56.630
because my son did it
and then i was worried

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:58.769
that people would judge
me if I tried to do it

00:05:58.769 --> 00:06:00.372
because I was worried about the judgment.

00:06:00.372 --> 00:06:01.571
I had to go out and do it.

00:06:01.571 --> 00:06:04.002
Or listening to music when
I'm walkin' in the street

00:06:04.002 --> 00:06:06.347
and dancing and then when I get to close

00:06:06.347 --> 00:06:07.743
to a busy intersection.

00:06:07.743 --> 00:06:08.934
Dancing smaller.

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:09.767
See that you catch it.

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:12.104
See you'll dance smaller just naturally.

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:15.268
You'll play smaller naturally.

00:06:15.268 --> 00:06:18.725
But if you can catch it
that's when you can say

00:06:18.725 --> 00:06:21.438
no I'm not impacting these people.

00:06:21.438 --> 00:06:24.651
I'm not tryin' to make
their life worse right?

00:06:24.651 --> 00:06:25.568
My dancing,

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:28.722
my doing whatever I
want to do in the street

00:06:28.722 --> 00:06:30.079
doesn't impact them.

00:06:30.079 --> 00:06:32.962
If anything it's giving them
something different to look at.

00:06:32.962 --> 00:06:34.031
It's bringing a little more joy.

00:06:34.031 --> 00:06:34.933
They might tell their co-worker

00:06:34.933 --> 00:06:36.661
they saw this crazy guy
on the street dancing.

00:06:36.661 --> 00:06:37.649
Maybe they go back to their office

00:06:37.649 --> 00:06:38.719
and dance a little bit more.

00:06:38.719 --> 00:06:41.186
Maybe what I'm doing is
actually inspiring them.

00:06:41.186 --> 00:06:44.025
But an actual baseball
so you can catch it.

00:06:44.025 --> 00:06:45.340
That's when you got to take the action.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:46.985
There's that great
expression of doing something

00:06:46.985 --> 00:06:50.937
everyday that scares you
but we don't actually do it.

00:06:50.937 --> 00:06:53.040
So I would encourage you

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.303
so when you feel that discomfort

00:06:55.303 --> 00:06:57.648
try to recognize it.

00:06:57.648 --> 00:07:01.314
Try to see it as this
is muscle building time

00:07:01.314 --> 00:07:03.002
and go out and do it.

00:07:03.002 --> 00:07:04.608
So the question today is I'm curious

00:07:04.608 --> 00:07:08.067
what was the last thing
you did that scared you?

00:07:08.067 --> 00:07:09.180
Leave it down in the comments below

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:10.542
I'm really curious to find out.

00:07:10.542 --> 00:07:12.675
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Priest Willis.

00:07:12.675 --> 00:07:15.230
Priest thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book.

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:16.463
Your One Word.

00:07:16.463 --> 00:07:17.901
I really appreciate the support

00:07:17.901 --> 00:07:20.038
and hope you enjoyed my book.

00:07:20.038 --> 00:07:21.439
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:07:21.439 --> 00:07:22.759
I believe in you.

00:07:22.759 --> 00:07:24.612
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:07:24.612 --> 00:07:26.942
and whatever your one word is.

00:07:26.942 --> 00:07:29.249
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:07:29.249 --> 00:07:31.666
for another shot of espresso.

00:07:32.544 --> 00:07:34.765
♫ I wake up every morning

00:07:34.765 --> 00:07:38.182
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:07:41.601 --> 00:07:44.364
- If I had to rewind the clock 10 years

00:07:44.364 --> 00:07:46.781
I would've insisted by people

00:07:47.657 --> 00:07:49.407
that are close to me,

00:07:50.516 --> 00:07:54.349
please push me into very unsafe projects.

00:07:54.349 --> 00:07:56.123
At least every other one.

00:07:56.123 --> 00:07:59.373
I think it's professionally responsible

00:08:00.449 --> 00:08:04.450
to not continue to remake the same role

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:05.604
over and over again.

00:08:05.604 --> 00:08:06.469
What's tonight?

00:08:06.469 --> 00:08:08.814
Turkey TV dinner, turkey TV dinner.

00:08:08.814 --> 00:08:10.170
[Interviewer] so it looks like you always

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:11.856
go out of your comfort zone right?

00:08:11.856 --> 00:08:14.081
Coming onto an island that
was completely deserted,

00:08:14.081 --> 00:08:16.633
no fresh water you didn't
even have the money to buy it

00:08:16.633 --> 00:08:19.395
and now you're sleeping
on a tent on the beach

00:08:19.395 --> 00:08:22.108
trying to figure out how
to get fresh water here.

00:08:22.108 --> 00:08:23.548
You do that often.

00:08:23.548 --> 00:08:24.780
You did it with the airline?

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:26.671
- I was just somebody that experienced

00:08:26.671 --> 00:08:29.552
the bad experience of
traveling on airlines.

00:08:29.552 --> 00:08:32.101
I was actually trying to get to the BVI,

00:08:32.101 --> 00:08:34.449
the British Virgin Islands
one day from Puerto Rico

00:08:34.449 --> 00:08:37.163
and the same lovely
lady was waiting for me

00:08:37.163 --> 00:08:38.189
and I'd been away for three weeks

00:08:38.189 --> 00:08:40.826
and American Airlines bumped the flight

00:08:40.826 --> 00:08:44.284
and so I went to the back of the airport

00:08:44.284 --> 00:08:45.617
I hired a plane.

00:08:46.564 --> 00:08:48.231
I had a black board.

00:08:49.074 --> 00:08:52.657
I wrote Virgin Airlines
one way $29 to BVI.

00:08:54.509 --> 00:08:56.029
Went around all the
people who had been bumped

00:08:56.029 --> 00:08:57.678
and I filled my first plane.

00:08:57.678 --> 00:08:59.734
And that got me thinking that airlines

00:08:59.734 --> 00:09:03.148
do bump people they don't care
about you or me particularly

00:09:03.148 --> 00:09:05.898
in the air so then rang up Boeing

00:09:07.386 --> 00:09:09.280
and said do you have any second N747's--

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:10.880
- No kidding I mean it was literally

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:12.280
that you just sat in the airport

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:13.352
and said I'm starting an airline right now

00:09:13.352 --> 00:09:14.379
because I'm frustrated.

00:09:14.379 --> 00:09:15.212
- Exactly.

00:09:15.212 --> 00:09:18.581
And I think most of the
best entrepreneurial ideas

00:09:18.581 --> 00:09:20.308
come out of frustration I think.

00:09:20.308 --> 00:09:24.087
If you're frustrated about something,

00:09:24.087 --> 00:09:25.365
the best way of sorting it out

00:09:25.365 --> 00:09:27.217
is get out and do it.

00:09:27.217 --> 00:09:28.906
And you've got yourself a business.

00:09:28.906 --> 00:09:30.462
- Starting with Lincoln
Lawyer was a time when I said

00:09:30.462 --> 00:09:33.549
I wanted to recalibrate my relationship

00:09:33.549 --> 00:09:34.617
with my career.

00:09:34.617 --> 00:09:35.450
I remember saying that.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:36.283
I remember thinking my career,

00:09:36.283 --> 00:09:37.116
I'm enjoying it.

00:09:37.116 --> 00:09:38.458
I love what it's given me.

00:09:38.458 --> 00:09:39.854
I like goin' to work.

00:09:39.854 --> 00:09:41.831
I like the things I've been doin'.

00:09:41.831 --> 00:09:42.776
But everything I started reading

00:09:42.776 --> 00:09:44.795
I felt like oh,

00:09:44.795 --> 00:09:46.850
it's another version
of something I've done

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.493
or I feel like I could do it next week

00:09:48.493 --> 00:09:49.678
and I remember going well wait a minute

00:09:49.678 --> 00:09:50.911
before you get mad at thinking

00:09:50.911 --> 00:09:52.680
you could do something next week,

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:54.038
that's a valid feeling.

00:09:54.038 --> 00:09:54.985
Don't just say no to something

00:09:54.985 --> 00:09:56.916
'cause you can feel like
you can naturally do it

00:09:56.916 --> 00:09:58.850
but then I said okay fair I'll shake

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:00.615
with you on that McConaughey but...

00:10:00.615 --> 00:10:03.131
(audience laughs)

00:10:03.131 --> 00:10:05.808
Let me find something that I don't know

00:10:05.808 --> 00:10:07.694
how what to do with that next week

00:10:07.694 --> 00:10:08.527
or the week after.

00:10:08.527 --> 00:10:09.706
Anytime something that I really like

00:10:09.706 --> 00:10:12.123
but I'm goin oh I'm not sure.

00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:15.251
That scares me that shakes my floor

00:10:15.251 --> 00:10:19.084
and I was fortunate
enough to that schedule F.

00:10:22.662 --> 00:10:24.266
Check I got in the Angels in the Outfield.

00:10:24.266 --> 00:10:25.706
Didn't know that my rent was paid.

00:10:25.706 --> 00:10:27.308
I was fortunate enough that
all my kids were going to eat.

00:10:27.308 --> 00:10:29.363
I was just shepherding my
first son into the world.

00:10:29.363 --> 00:10:31.951
So I had that to take care of my time.

00:10:31.951 --> 00:10:33.801
I said it's a great time
to go in the shadows

00:10:33.801 --> 00:10:36.846
and be a father and sit back

00:10:36.846 --> 00:10:39.068
and see if something turns
you on from the inside

00:10:39.068 --> 00:10:40.179
or if something finds you

00:10:40.179 --> 00:10:42.736
if you're the target.

00:10:42.736 --> 00:10:43.889
We're okay rent's paid.

00:10:43.889 --> 00:10:44.880
Kids are going to eat.

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:46.650
We can take some time off.

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:48.794
I in know way was
thinking about oh I'm done

00:10:48.794 --> 00:10:49.824
but I didn't know how long the dry spell

00:10:49.824 --> 00:10:52.378
was going to go so I said
no to some of the things

00:10:52.378 --> 00:10:54.512
that were similar to what
I had been doing before

00:10:54.512 --> 00:10:56.568
and it took awhile I had
to sit down with my agent

00:10:56.568 --> 00:10:58.703
and say hey I'm really going to do this

00:10:58.703 --> 00:11:00.516
and I need your help with
my commitment to this

00:11:00.516 --> 00:11:03.236
because after eight months

00:11:03.236 --> 00:11:05.783
if the same thing comes in
with a big 10 million dollar

00:11:05.783 --> 00:11:08.580
paycheck it starts to
read better and funnier.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:11.665
(audience laughs)

00:11:11.665 --> 00:11:13.307
I promise you.

00:11:13.307 --> 00:11:15.140
I mean the same words.

00:11:18.161 --> 00:11:21.131
All the sudden I think this thing's great.

00:11:21.131 --> 00:11:23.644
(audience laughs)

00:11:23.644 --> 00:11:25.121
I think I can find an angle.

00:11:25.121 --> 00:11:27.588
No I can make it a
different experience for me.

00:11:27.588 --> 00:11:29.193
So I said I'm going to need your help

00:11:29.193 --> 00:11:32.449
bunkering down there and
saying no to some things

00:11:32.449 --> 00:11:34.380
and so I'm going to need
you to be a gate keeper

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:35.407
one to keep from getting to me,

00:11:35.407 --> 00:11:38.655
two let's be real clear I'm lookin'

00:11:38.655 --> 00:11:40.714
for some different things to do.

00:11:40.714 --> 00:11:42.894
He holed up he handled that.

00:11:42.894 --> 00:11:45.565
My wife we said we don't know
how long it's going to be dry

00:11:45.565 --> 00:11:47.914
then after they quit sending those,

00:11:47.914 --> 00:11:48.747
then it did get dry.

00:11:48.747 --> 00:11:50.629
Then nothing came for about year.

00:11:50.629 --> 00:11:51.962
There's nothing.

00:11:53.594 --> 00:11:55.323
I didn't have any sleepless nights

00:11:55.323 --> 00:11:56.156
or oh my gosh.

00:11:56.156 --> 00:11:57.752
I was like no I'll find something.

00:11:57.752 --> 00:11:58.945
I'll write.

00:11:58.945 --> 00:12:00.055
I was writing a lot.

00:12:00.055 --> 00:12:01.699
I was turning myself on creatively

00:12:01.699 --> 00:12:04.168
and as I said I had my first
son to shepherd into the world.

00:12:04.168 --> 00:12:06.057
And then the funny thing happened.

00:12:06.057 --> 00:12:08.315
The beautiful thing happened

00:12:08.315 --> 00:12:09.920
that I somehow I was the target,

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:12.469
drew the arrow and I think my opinion is

00:12:12.469 --> 00:12:16.136
I became a new good
idea by removing myself.

00:12:18.947 --> 00:12:21.088
I became William Frincken calls,

00:12:21.088 --> 00:12:22.859
Steven Soderberg calls for the first time.

00:12:22.859 --> 00:12:25.821
Somehow in that two years
I became fresh new idea

00:12:25.821 --> 00:12:29.810
that I don't think I was
two, three years prior.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.152
How that works I'm not sure because

00:12:31.152 --> 00:12:33.015
I didn't send a memo out.

00:12:33.015 --> 00:12:35.689
(audience laughs)

